The document/key storage data types and the DataStorageService /
SecureKeyStorage protocols are reimplemented in Cangjie with the original Swift
sources used as the reference implementation. The iOS Keychain storage backend
(KeyChainStorageService / KeyChainSecureKeyStorage) is replaced on HarmonyOS by
an encrypted RelationalStore (RDB) document backend and HUKS-backed key storage,
since HarmonyOS has no drop-in equivalent of the iOS Keychain.

This product depends on and/or bundles the following third-party software:

  - eudi_lib_mdoc_data_model (Apache-2.0; pinned third_party clone) — credential
    data model (Document / DocClaim / SecureArea protocol) types.
  - eudi_lib_core_crypto (pinned third_party clone) — HUKS-backed key
    capabilities used by the secure key storage layer.
  - eudi_lib_cbor (Apache-2.0; pinned third_party clone) — CBOR encoding.
  - cangjie-stdx 1.1.3.1 (Apache-2.0) — bundled under entry/libs/stdx/;
    stdx.crypto provides AES / secure random / digest primitives.
  - OpenSSL runtime libraries (libcrypto_openssl.z.so, libssl_openssl.z.so)
    and libsecurec.so, bundled under entry/libs/arm64-v8a/ for on-device
    stdx.crypto / HUKS execution.

